<!----- FILE help/eng.md START ----->
<h1 id="module-about">About</h1>
<h2 id="version"></h2>
Author: Fast Light [Margin.Top](https://margin.top/vsfile)
QQ: 12613497 Email: [fastlight@margin.top](mailto:fastlight@margin.top)
GitHub project: [https://github.com/FastLight126/vsfile](https://github.com/FastLight126/vsfile)
Report bugs or suggestions: [https://github.com/FastLight126/vsfile/issues](https://github.com/FastLight126/vsfile/issues)
<h1 id="module-start">Quick start</h1>
<h2 id="start">Basic operations</h2>
Use the explorer on the left to browse directories and tabs on the right to view and manage files. Double-click a folder to enter it or a file to open it in a suitable viewer.
<h2 id="navigation">Directory navigation</h2>
- Use the path bar to return to any parent directory or enter a path directly.
- Use Back, Forward, and Up to browse your location history.
- The explorer and folder pages synchronize after files change.
<h1 id="module-files">File management</h1>
<h2 id="files">Files and folders</h2>
The toolbar and context menu provide create, upload, download, rename, delete, refresh, and copy-path actions. Hold `Shift` for a range selection. Read-only users cannot use modifying actions.
<h2 id="upload">Uploading files</h2>
Choose files with Upload or drag them onto a folder page. Progress appears in the toolbar. For name conflicts, choose Overwrite, Discard, or Rename.
<h2 id="clipboard">Cut, copy, and paste</h2>
Cut or copy selected items, open the destination, then paste. Copying within one directory creates a uniquely named duplicate; cross-directory conflicts prompt for an action.
<h2 id="archive">Compress and extract</h2>
Create zip or tar.gz archives and extract them into the current directory or a new matching directory. Menus are hidden when the format is unsupported, the user is read-only, or write rules block it.
<h1 id="module-viewers">Editor and viewers</h1>
<h2 id="viewers">Opening files</h2>
Text opens in the code editor. The image viewer supports zoom, rotation, flipping, inversion, and dragging. Audio and video use built-in players and stop when you leave the page.
<h2 id="display">View, sort, and filter</h2>
Folders support Details, Icons, Tiles, and Gallery views. Details can be sorted and filtered by name, size, type, creation time, or modification time. Each directory remembers its view.
<h2 id="permissions">Permissions</h2>
The bottom bar shows size and permissions. Writable users can enter a three-digit mode or use the permission matrix for selected items. This setting may be unavailable on Windows.
<h1 id="module-account">Account and two-factor authentication</h1>
<h2 id="account">Account management</h2>
Select the current user in the top bar to view account details, change the password, or configure TOTP. Keep the authenticator secret in a safe place.
<h1 id="module-userinfo">User profile changes</h1>
<h2 id="user-password">Passwords and TOTP</h2>
New users need a password; existing users can leave it blank to keep the current password. TOTP can be enabled or disabled per user, and the authenticator secret must be kept secure.
<h2 id="user-totp">Two-factor authentication</h2>
TOTP two-factor authentication adds an extra layer of security to the current account. After enabling it, a 6-digit code from the authenticator is required when signing in. If the code or secret is lost, contact an administrator to reset it.
<h1 id="module-users" class="admin">User management</h1>
<h2 id="users">User list</h2>
Administrators can add, remove, and edit users from the settings page. Each user has an independent access directory, write rules, and TOTP settings.
<h2 id="user-admin-ban">Admin edit restriction</h2>
To prevent accidental changes, administrators cannot edit their own information here. If you need to edit it, create another administrator account and sign in with that administrator account.
<h2 id="user-readonly">Read-only and admin</h2>
Read-only users can browse files but cannot modify them; administrators manage configuration and user lists. One user cannot be both read-only and administrator.
<h2 id="user-directory">User directory</h2>
Each user has a root directory that controls access scope and write permissions. The path may be relative or absolute, and separate directories per user are recommended to prevent unauthorized access.
<h2 id="user-write-limit">Write restrictions</h2>
Single-file size limits and extension allowlists/denylists control upload and write behavior. After changing these rules, administrators should confirm that required files remain available.
<h1 id="module-config" class="admin">Basic configuration</h1>
<h2 id="config-default-lang">Default language</h2>
The interface language used for new users or when the browser has no saved language choice. A language selected from the top navigation takes precedence.
<h2 id="config-timezone">Timezone</h2>
Used to display and calculate dates, times, and log information. Enter a valid timezone name and select it from the suggestions.
<h2 id="config-upload-limit">Single-file upload limit</h2>
Accepts integers and B/K/KB/M/MB/G/GB/T/TB/P/PB/E/EB/Z/ZB/Y/YB units. Values without a unit are bytes.
<h2 id="config-write-limit">Write restrictions</h2>
An allowlist permits only listed extensions; a blocklist rejects listed extensions. Separate extensions with commas. `?` represents files without an extension. When an allowlist is configured, the blocklist is ignored.
<h2 id="config-totp-fix">TOTP validation window</h2>
Use a non-negative integer: 0 disables the window, 1 allows plus or minus 30 seconds, 2 allows plus or minus 60 seconds, and so on.
<h2 id="config-session-name">Session name</h2>
Usually does not need changing. A change resets all sessions and client-side saved settings.
<h2 id="config-cache-time">Cache duration</h2>
HTTP cache duration for static resources in seconds. Set it to 0 to disable caching.
<h2 id="config-main-password">Main password</h2>
Used to create and read download tokens. Changing it invalidates every existing download token.
<h2 id="config-comment">Comment</h2>
Stores deployment notes or other administrative information and does not affect file operations.
